    816  f10c				   .Line
    817  f10c							; --- Player sprite: color for THIS line, graphics byte for NEXT line ---
    818  f10c							; GRP0 written on line S displays on line S+1 (latched at the sprite's
    819  f10c							; window start after the write) — index graphics with A0+1 ($ff wraps
    820  f10c							; to 0 = row0 on the line before the sprite).
    821  f10c							; Running-Y: Y = A0 = Scanline - RoomY is computed ONCE at kernel entry
    822  f10c							; (sec/sbc RoomY/tay); .Line's iny advances it (Y = A0+1 after the
    823  f10c							; graphics write = A0 of the next line). Nothing between rows may touch
    824  f10c							; Y — the water-strip band-color read is an inlined `lda` (Y untouched).
    825  f10c							; Cycle budget — MEASURED (sim_frame_budget, bugs.md #29 Class A):
    826  f10c							; the old worst path (in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range) was
    827  f10c							; 78c: WSYNC write landed 2c into the next line -> full-line stall ->
    828  f10c							; +1 scanline on every frame whose object window overlapped the A0=11
    829  f10c							; line (24 stalls in the SIM_LEVEL=2 window, always even frames —
    830  f10c							; SelectActiveObject parity rotation). Root fix: the color/beam gate
    831  f10c							; below stops at A0=10; row 11 inherits row 10's COLUP0/ENAM0 writes
    832  f10c							; (PlayerColTable/BeamMask [10]==[11], verify_build asserts) because
    833  f10c							; GRP0 row11 is fetched on line A0=10 already ("row11 shows via
    834  f10c							; line10"). Worst path measured 2026-10-15 (vcrunch jitter hunt):
    835  f10c							; in-window color/beam/GRP0 + object in-range = 69c between WSs,
    836  f10c							; start-to-start d=72 — was 73/76 (= stall zone 74-76, whole-screen
    837  f10c							; +1-line jitter) until the dead `cpy #12 / bcs .GrpZero` (4c, never
    838  f10c							; taken on the A0<=10 color path) moved to .GrpSkip. Budget: work
    839  f10c							; <= 70c / d <= 73 — a 74-76 segment stalls a full scanline.
    840  f10c							; ObjSprites+71 must stay in the $FExx page (else lda ObjSprites,X
    841  f10c							; page-crosses, +1c on the GRP1 fetch) — verify_build enforces this.
    842  f10c							; Branch targets all same-page (3c taken) and BeamMask operand in $FExx
    843  f10c							; (4c fetch, no-cross — verify_build S2.2 guard).
    844  f10c							; GRP1 object section clobbers X (ObjSprites index) — row counter lives in
    845  f10c							; RowIdx and X is reloaded after bne. Row-advance +6c on the .Row setup
    846  f10c							; scanline (segment 63c -> 69c <= 76c): frame length unchanged.
    847  f10c							; The old Scanline/sec/sbc/tay prefix cost 10c more (body 66c -> WSYNC
    848  f10c							; write on cycle 76 = one cycle late): WSYNC stalled a full line per
    849  f10c							; overlapping scanline — stretched cave row, HUD pushed down, and with
    850  f10c							; GRP1 flicker rotation the frame length alternated (one-tile oscillation).
    851  f10c							; Keep the hot path at <= 70c work: an overrun duplicates the scanline.
    852  f10c		       c0 0b		      cpy	#PLAYER_SPRITE_H - 1
    853  f10e		       b0 40		      bcs	.GrpSkip	; A0 >= 11 (incl $ff): no color/beam this line.
    854  f110							; A0=11 skips too (Class-A stall line): rows
    855  f110							; 10/11 share color+beam bytes, so row 10's
    856  f110							; writes are still in effect here.
    857  f110		       b9 f5 f8 	      lda	PlayerColTable,Y	; 4c — per-row color from ROM
    858  f113		       85 06		      sta	COLUP0	; COLUP0 has no latch: applies to this line
    859  f115							; --- Laser S2.2: ENAM0 = beam mask for THIS line (in-window only) ---
    860  f115							; BeamMask = {0,0,2,0,0...} → ENAM0 on RoomY+2 only (single yellow
    861  f115							; strip — user directive 2026-10-08: the red row-3 strip is gone;
    862  f115							; kill window in LaserHitTestBody keeps rows RoomY+2..3 = superset).
    863  f115							; In-window path is the only safe place (Y<11 guaranteed); outside the
    864  f115							; window ENAM0 keeps its last in-window write ($00 at A0=10) — no HUD
    865  f115							; artifact. Table lives in $FExx (no-cross = 4c, verify_build guard).
