   3473  fdd1							; BombEnemyBlast — bank2 entry tramp ($FDD8, lamp-safe S9 2026-10-07): the
   3474  fdd1							; BombTick `jsr` lands here (bank0), `sta $1FF8` switches to bank2, the `jmp`
   3475  fdd1							; is fetched from bank2's byte-identical mirror at this same address and
   3476  fdd1							; lands on the body at $FD87 (the lamp type-check reads enemy records that
   3477  fdd1							; live in bank2). Body tail-jmps ReturnPad ($FBF8); A = 1 kill (BombTick
   3478  fdd1							; awards +50 — pads cannot nest), 0 none. Old inline body ($F87F, 66B)
   3479  fdd1							; deleted: the region re-packs into the gap before the $FBD6 fold pin
   3480  fdd1							; (pre-pad headroom stays 1B — pins absorb upstream shrink, not the org).
   3481  fdd1							; TWIN: bank2.asm mirrors these exact 6 bytes at $FDD8 (the pad after
   3482  fdd1							; .HOVdone). The PickPlayerFrame pin that used to absorb the size is gone
   3483  fdd1							; (retired 2026-10-20); the $FC49 / $FBF8 pins bound this block today.
   3484  fdd1							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   3485  fdd1		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$FDD8 - *, 0	; pin: bank2's blast-tramp mirror is at $FDD8
   3486  fdd8				   BombEnemyBlast
   3487  fdd8		       8d f8 1f 	      sta	$1FF8
   3488  fddb		       4c 87 fd 	      jmp	$FD87	; BombEnemyBlastBody (bank2.lst — after
   3489  fdde							;   .HOVfeature; NOT in the TitleJetColors
   3490  fdde							;   span)
   3491  fdde							;   (2026-10-13: was $FD79 — crush-kill b6
   3492  fdde							;   latch + feature gate pushed +14; same day
   3493  fdde							;   was $FD6C — .HOVfeature pushed +13; 2026-
   3494  fdde							;   10-10: was $FD6B — 1-byte stale operand =
   3495  fdde							;   entry mid-instruction at `lda EnemyCount+1`;
   3496  fdde							;   garbage path's `inc $4A,X` set wall bits
   3497  fdde							;   via $CA)
